      "justification": "This is the larger of the two defender clusters, holding 98 of the 136 eligible defenders, and it is defined by what is absent rather than by any positive signature. All eight of its most distinguishing features are negative deviations from the defender mean: key passes per 90 sit 0.44 standard deviations below it, assists per 90 0.42 standard deviations below, expected assists per 90 0.42 standard deviations below, crosses per 90 0.36 standard deviations below and shots per 90 0.31 standard deviations below. Nothing in the eighteen features sits materially above the defender average, the largest positive deviation being only 0.04 standard deviations, so the honest description is low attacking involvement rather than a defensive speciality. That limitation is a property of the data and not of the players, because the withdrawal of the Opta-derived tables left no tackling detail, no pressing, no aerial duels and no ball recoveries with which a defender could be described positively. The members closest to the centroid are Calvin Bassey, Emmanuel Agbadou, Jan Paul van Hecke and Max Kilman, who are central defenders in the conventional sense. The split is provisional: bootstrap resampling of the defender scope gives a mean adjusted Rand index of 0.582, the lowest of the four scopes analysed and far below the global figure of 0.908, so the boundary between the two defender clusters moves substantially under resampling even though the direction of the contrast does not.",
