      "justification": "The smaller defender cluster, 38 of 136 eligible defenders, is defined by wide attacking output, and all eight of its distinguishing features are positive. Key passes per 90 sit 1.14 standard deviations above the defender mean, assists per 90 1.09 standard deviations above, expected assists per 90 1.08 standard deviations above, crosses per 90 0.92 standard deviations above and shots per 90 0.79 standard deviations above, with tackles won per 90 also 0.61 standard deviations above the mean. Because the deviations are one-sided this is the high involvement end of a single dominant contrast rather than a separate tactical instruction, and the players it selects are full backs and wing backs: Malo Gusto, Djed Spence, Pervis Estupiñán, Milos Kerkez and Reece James are the members closest to the centroid. The label describes output and not intent, since the surviving features cannot separate a defender who is asked to overlap from one who plays in a team that crosses often. Bootstrap stability for the defender scope is a mean adjusted Rand index of 0.582 with a standard deviation of 0.221 and a minimum of 0.018 across 200 resamples, so the membership of this cluster should be read as indicative rather than settled.",
