      "justification": "The second midfield cluster, 87 players, is the mirror of the first and is the high involvement side of the midfield contrast. Its centroid sits 0.75 standard deviations above the midfield mean on shots on target per 90, 0.72 standard deviations above on non-penalty expected goals per 90, 0.71 standard deviations above on shots per 90, 0.67 standard deviations above on expected assists per 90 and 0.64 standard deviations above on key passes per 90, while interceptions per 90 are 0.60 standard deviations below the mean and tackles won per 90 0.48 standard deviations below it. Shooting and creation load on the same side of the split, which means the eighteen surviving features cannot separate a midfielder who scores from one who supplies, and no such distinction is claimed here. The members closest to the centroid are Morgan Gibbs-White, Dejan Kulusevski, Kaoru Mitoma, Morgan Rogers and Amad Diallo, a set that mixes central attacking midfielders with wide midfielders and so cuts across the listed position strings. Bootstrap stability for the midfield scope is a mean adjusted Rand index of 0.837, the strongest of the three position groups and close to the global figure of 0.908.",
